# Architecture Decision Records

How {{ project_name }} records its decisions: one short Markdown file per decision, kept in this folder and changed in
the same pull request as the code it explains.

## When to Write One

Write a record for a non-obvious choice that someone would otherwise question again: a design with real alternatives,
a trade-off that looks wrong without its reasons, or a departure from the project template. The conventions themselves
go in `AGENTS.md` or the instruction files it lists; a record explains why a convention is what it is. `/analyze-decision`
compares the options and writes one.

## How to Write One

- Copy [0000-template.md](0000-template.md) to `NNNN-kebab-case-title.md`, with the next free number, starting from
  `0001`.
- The status is `Proposed` while the decision is open, `Accepted` once it holds, and `Superseded by NNNN` when a later
  record replaces it.
- Never rewrite the decision of an accepted record. A changed decision is a new record that supersedes the old one, and
  the old one's status says so. Fixing a typo or a broken link is fine.
- Add the record to the index below.

## The Template's Decisions

The project template's own decisions are in [project-template/](project-template/README.md). Template updates replace
that folder. To decide otherwise, write a record here that says "Supersedes project-template ADR-NNNN" and list the
override in `AGENTS.md`.

